{
  "$comment": [
    "Curated data-centre projects, transcribed from four public trackers.",
    "",
    "FracTracker's FOIA permit file is the spine of this layer, but it records",
    "mostly small enterprise server rooms and carries no status or capacity. The",
    "hyperscale build-out -- Rosemount, Becker, Chisago, Monticello -- is not in",
    "it at all. This file holds what four public trackers say about those",
    "projects, and is refreshed by pull request, not by a scraper.",
    "",
    "THIS LAYER IS CONTEXTUAL, NOT AUTHORITATIVE. It exists because data centres",
    "are the physical substrate the surveillance systems on this map run on, and",
    "because they impose local costs -- power, water, land, tax abatements --",
    "that give people a reason to show up to a council meeting. It is not a",
    "facility registry and must not be cited as one.",
    "",
    "RULES",
    "",
    "1. Every fact lives under `asserts`, keyed by the source that says it. There",
    "   is no unattributed field. If no source says it, it is not here.",
    "2. The sources disagree. That is recorded, not resolved: where they claim",
    "   different statuses the ingest marks the record disputed, takes the most",
    "   conservative claim, and the detail panel prints what each source said.",
    "3. Location is a `city` or a `county` name, never a hand-typed coordinate.",
    "   The ingest resolves it against the Census jurisdiction index, so the",
    "   point and the county come from a federal record rather than from us.",
    "   `coordinates` may be given only where a public record identifies the",
    "   actual parcel; then set `locationPrecision` to \"site\".",
    "4. The trackers' own county column is unreliable -- MoreThanJustParks files",
    "   UnitedHealth Minnetonka under Sherburne and Stream Minneapolis under",
    "   Carver. We ignore it and derive county from the resolved point.",
    "5. Entries describe companies, facilities and proposals. Never a person.",
    "",
    "Status values: operating, under-construction, proposed, cancelled, withdrawn.",
    "Conservative ordering for conflicts: proposed < under-construction < operating."
  ],

  "sources": {
    "mtjp": {
